From ca064e5f7011e03e94cb2112f48952edfc3114cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:16:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): native git-hook fallback so TDD enforcement is
 never silently inert (B3)

The live `forge setup` path (bin/forge.js executeSetup -> installGitHooks) had
diverged from the fixed copy in lib/commands/setup.js: it still had the stub-shadow
bug, copied the repo's OWN dev lefthook.yml (which references repo-internal scripts/
a user project lacks), had no native fallback when the lefthook binary was
unavailable, and never verified hooks were active. Result: after a clean
`forge setup`, TDD enforcement was silently inert and `forge ship` then hard-blocked
on a missing hook (kernel e452422c / c713fce7 / 22e33dbf, beta blocker B3).

- New lib/lefthook-wiring.js: single source of truth shared by bin/forge.js and
  lib/commands/setup.js so the two copies can never drift again. Exports the real
  user lefthook.yml, the stub-shadow guard, a native .git/hooks installer
  (resolves worktree gitdirs; preserves/backs-up pre-existing non-Forge hooks),
  and an honest verifyHooksActive().
- installGitHooks now: writes the REAL config (never the repo dev config nor the
  stock example), installs lefthook when available, falls back to native
  .git/hooks otherwise, and verifies LOUDLY (non-zero exit) if enforcement is
  still not active - never a silent no-op.
- autoInstallLefthook refuses to `npm install --save-dev lefthook` when the
  project has no package.json (would resolve against an ancestor - 22e33dbf);
  native hooks back enforcement instead.
- lib/commands/setup.js repair path converged onto the shared module and gains the
  same native fallback + verify (warns, never sets exit code - runs mid-stage).
- cli-lifecycle reinstall test updated: reinstall = reset + fresh setup, so it now
  correctly leaves a reinstalled .forge (asserts the old empty marker is gone).

